      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Both approaches offer distinct leverage points, as strengthened enforcement reduces immediate border pressure while certification pathways drive long-term economic integration and demographic stability. A hybrid strategy that combines robust security measures with streamlined humanitarian processing often yields the most resilient outcomes by addressing both root causes and immediate consequences of migration crises. Ultimately, the choice depends on whether the committee prioritizes immediate border control metrics or broader societal benefits like workforce development and reduced human suffering.",
