      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Prioritizing pathways to citizenship is significantly more sustainable economically because it directly expands the formal workforce, boosts tax revenue, and integrates migrants into the social safety net, which enforcement alone cannot achieve. While high-tech border security provides necessary short-term disruption, it fails to address structural labor deficits often needed by a growing economy and can exacerbate social friction by criminalizing migration. Therefore, from a long-term stability perspective, investment in humanitarian processing and legal integration is objectively more pragmatic than relying solely on enforcement measures that do not alter underlying demographic trends.",
